I had the same problem as @renestalder. 
The problem was not really connected to `nuxt-apollo`, however I drop the problem analysis here, in case someone else will have the same problem in the future.

For our components we stored the initial data in a global constant, which we then returned in the `data()` function:
```js
const initialData = {...};
export default Vue.extend({
  data(): Data {
    return initialData;
  },
});
```

Since we returned `intialData` directly, Vue took the `initialData` object for the components data. So every component of every request shared the same `data` instance.
Now, when a component is mounted, `vue-apollo` will check if there is already a data property for every smart query or not. If not, it will create a property with a getter-only, which returns an internal property. 

So in our case, for the first request, Vue Apollo created a getter-only property on the components data. As the components data was the same object as the `initialData` instance, during the second request, our `intialData` already had a property for the smart-query, which was getter only. So when setting a result, Vue Apollo tried to set the data-property directly on the components data-property.

Returning a copy of `initialData` in our component solved the problem:

```js
const initialData = {...};
export default Vue.extend({
  data(): Data {
    return {...initialData};
  },
}
```


As reference, the implied code of Vue Apollo is here: https://github.com/vuejs/vue-apollo/blob/19482fa199a9de25a40e91ad15e98225652acbb0/packages/vue-apollo/src/smart-query.js#L195

I found an option how to use `@vue/apollo-composable`. Need to perform a couple of simple steps:
Install `@vue/apollo-composable`, create plugin `provide-apollo-client.ts` (name can be any) with the following content:
```js
// plugins/provide-apollo-client.js
import { provide } from '@vue/composition-api';
import { DefaultApolloClient } from '@vue/apollo-composable';

export default ({ app }) => {
	app.setup = () => {
		const apolloClient = app.apolloProvider.defaultClient;

		provide(DefaultApolloClient, apolloClient);
	}
}
```
Specify it in the config with the main API
```js
// nuxt.config.js
plugins: [
	'@/plugins/composition-api',
	'@/plugins/provide-apollo-client'
],
```
The rest of the configuration is no different. However, there are still unsolved problems with SSR errors (example: 404 status code).

@negezor I think assigning `app.setup = () => { ... }` could be a problem if more than one Nuxt plugin want to customize `app.setup` ... i.e. this is not composable in itself and raises a TS error `Type '() => void' is not assignable to type 'SetupFunction<Data, Data>'.`

Maybe injecting apolloClient the usual "nuxt way" could work ... I also asked a related [question](https://discordapp.com/channels/473401852243869706/496688443141652500/703617526470410290) on Discord.

This points to a missing feature of Nuxt for making plugins work nicely with the Composition API.

Following @negezor's plugin, (@lewebsimple and in a more nuxy way via [nuxt-composition-api](https://github.com/nuxt-community/apollo-module/issues/288)):

```typescript
// ~/plugins/apollo/provide.ts
import { provide, reactive } from "nuxt-composition-api";
import { Context, Plugin } from "@nuxt/types";
import { ApolloClients } from "@vue/apollo-composable";

const provideApollo: Plugin = ({ app }: Context) => {
  app.setup = () => {
    // since plugin is eval'd after module app.apolloProvider will always be defined
    const clients = reactive(app.apolloProvider?.clients); 
    provide(DefaultApolloClient, clients?.defaultClient);
    // not functionally important but req'd return type
    return { [ApolloClients]: clients }; 
  };
};

export default provideApollo;
```

One important thing to note is that `@vue/apollo-composable` expects a config named `default`, whereas `@nuxtjs/apollo`'s default config is named `defaultClient`. If you provide `ApolloClients` vs. `DefaultApolloClient`, you must use `{ clientId: "defaultConfig" }` as an option when calling `apollo-composeable`.
 
```vue
<template>
  {{ result.company.name }}
</template>
<script lang="ts">
  import { Component, Vue } from "nuxt-property-decorator";
  import "vue-apollo"; // just noticed this is here, don't recall why...
  import { useCompanyQuery } from "@/generated/graphql-codegen";

  @Component({
    setup: () => {
      const { result, loading, error } = useCompanyQuery({
        where: { isParent: true }
      });

      return { result, loading, error };
    }
  })
  export default class CompaniesCard extends Vue {}
</script>
```

NB: Companies and Company are different queries.

~For fluency's sake `defaultClient` needs to be renamed `default` for interop. with `@vue/apollo-composable`.~

**Edit:** Weirdly enough vue-apollo [_does_ use `defaultClient`](https://github.com/vuejs/vue-apollo/blob/b13d688a99f1233dad659253e9f1f85b7ef1c10e/packages/vue-apollo/src/apollo-provider.js#L8), and `@vue/apollo-composeable` [uses a different property name](https://v4.apollo.vuejs.org/guide-composable/setup.html#multiple-clients).

