Are you running the GraphQL server and your UI server together on port 8000? That's what this approach of using both `httpEndpoint` and `browserHttpEndpoint` assumes.

For example, in a project I use [`nuxt.render`](https://nuxtjs.org/api/nuxt-render) to run Nuxt and my GraphQL API in the same Express app / server. It looks something like this:

``` js
const express = require("express");
const middleware = require("./middleware");
const graphqlServer = require("./graphql");
const nuxtServer = require("./nuxt");

const app = express();

app.use(middleware);
app.use("/graphql", graphqlServer);
app.use(nuxtServer);

app.listen(process.env.PORT);
```

