issues.body:
### Description

In development, the DevTools page that the module registers (`/__better-auth-devtools`) leaks its styles into the host app.

The page has an unscoped `<style>` block with global selectors, for example:

```css
*{box-sizing:border-box}
body{margin:0}
button,input{font:inherit}
input{background:var(--ba-bg);border:1px solid var(--ba-border);padding:7px 10px;width:min(340px,100%)}
button:hover:not(:disabled){background:var(--ba-hover)}
h2{border-bottom:1px solid var(--ba-border);font-size:13px;padding:10px 12px}
table, th, td { ... }
```

In `nuxt dev` the stylesheet of this page ends up on every page of the app (it is linked in the SSR HTML of regular pages), so these rules override the app's own styles: `h2` headings become 13px with a bottom border, text inputs get a fixed width and padding, checkbox layouts break, icon buttons get a background on hover.

Production builds are not affected, since the page is registered only in development.

### Reproduction

1. Nuxt app with Tailwind (or any styles for `h2`, `input`, `button`), `@nuxtjs/better-auth` in `modules`.
2. Run `nuxt dev` and open any page with an `h2` heading.
3. In DevTools → Elements, the computed `font-size` of the `h2` comes from `h2 { ... font-size: 13px ... }` of `__better-auth-devtools.vue`; the `<link>` to `pages/__better-auth-devtools.vue?vue&type=style...` is present in the page head.

### Expected

DevTools page styles do not affect the host app, e.g. `<style scoped>` or all selectors nested under `.devtools-shell`.

### Workaround

Remove the page from the routes in `nuxt.config.ts`:

```ts
hooks: {
  'pages:resolved'(pages) {
    const index = pages.findIndex(page => page.name === 'better-auth-devtools')
    if (index !== -1) pages.splice(index, 1)
  },
},
```

### Versions

- `@nuxtjs/better-auth` 0.3.9 (also present in `main`, `src/runtime/app/pages/__better-auth-devtools.vue`)
- `better-auth` 1.7.7
- `nuxt` 4.6.0, Vite 8, Node 24.15

The global styles seem to come from #369, where the page moved to its own CSS.

