Hello guys! I found this issue a few days ago while searching for solution. Although it may not be relevant since I'm not familiar with Vue.js and Nuxt, I want to share what I found. First you should know that I'm developing NextJS app. I found out that the problem is happening because of the StrictMode of React being enabled by default and component's code was executed twice in development environment.

One of the solutions was to turn this StrictMode off and the other may help you too here, because it is not React specific. This is the code that fixed the issue:

`
useEffect(() => {
    try {
      (window as any).adsbygoogle = (window as any).adsbygoogle || [];
      if ((window as any).adsbygoogle.loaded === false) {
        (window as any).adsbygoogle.push({});
      }
    } catch (error: any) {
      console.error(error.message);
    }
  }, []);
`

There is property on `adsbygoogle` object which is called `loaded`. You can use it's value to check if there is already object being pushed in this array and prevent calling the push() method more than once. I hope this help you fixing the issue. Please let me know if it works for you too. Good luck! :)

