approach of @skarnl worked for Universal Rendering, but not to the full extent with SSG.

### Universal Rendering (Node.js Server)
With Universal Rendering it's possible to redirect user according to their i18n cookie or browser setting. It is dynamic and very low overhead:

```ts
// nuxt.config.ts
  i18n: {
    strategy: 'prefix_and_default',
    detectBrowserLanguage: {
      useCookie: true,
    },
    defaultLocale: 'en',
  },
```

```ts
// redirect-root.global.ts
export default defineNuxtRouteMiddleware((to) => {
  const { $i18n } = useNuxtApp();

  if (to.path === '/') {
    const defaultLocale =
      $i18n.getLocaleCookie() ||
      $i18n.getBrowserLocale() ||
      $i18n.defaultLocale;
    return navigateTo(`/${defaultLocale}`);
  }
});

```

### SSG (aka nuxi generate or nuxi build --prerender)

With SSG this middleware runs at build time and there is no way to detect the users i18n cookie or browser language. When generating the index.html page nuxt then falls back to redirecting all users to the defaultLocale. This is better than no redirect but is sertainly not optimal, since the whole i18n cookie or browser language get ignored also for returning clients. SSG One thing I had to adapt, was hinting to nitro prerenderer which routes are available so that SSG was working as intended:

```ts
// nuxt.config.ts
  i18n: {
    strategy: 'prefix_and_default',
    detectBrowserLanguage: {
      useCookie: true,
    },
    defaultLocale: 'en',
  },
nitro: {
    prerender: {
      routes: ['/en', '/fr', '/de'],
    },
  },
```

As stated, this will generate a static redirect to defaultLocale
```html
<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url=/en"></head></html>
```

### Improved SSG

I've used the approach of @steffenstolze to improve this redirect behaviour with some js. 
For this to work, we don't set a defaultLocale. No redirect middleware.
This is probably quite bad for SEO. 

```ts
// nuxt.config.ts
  i18n: {
    strategy: 'prefix',
    defaultLocale: undefined,
    detectBrowserLanguage: {
      useCookie: true,
    },
  },
    nitro: {
      static: true,
      // Hacky approach to redirect create index.html file for root redirect
      hooks: {
        'prerender:generate'(route, nitro) {
          if (route?.route === '/200.html') {
            const redirectHtml = readFileSync('redirect.html', 'utf-8');
            const outputPath = path.join(
              nitro.options.output.publicDir,
              'index.html',
            );
            writeFileSync(outputPath, redirectHtml);
          }
        },
      },
      prerender: {
        routes: ['/de', '/fr', '/en'],
      },
    },
```

```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title></title>
    <script>
      function getCookieValue(cookieName) {
        // Parse document.cookie to find the desired cookie
        const cookies = document.cookie.split('; ');
        for (const cookie of cookies) {
          const [name, value] = cookie.split('=');
          if (name === cookieName) {
            return value;
          }
        }
        return;
      }

      function getLocale() {
        const localeCookie = getCookieValue('i18n_redirected');

        if (localeCookie) return localeCookie;

        const browserLanguage = navigator.language;

        if (browserLanguage.includes('de')) {
          return 'de';
        } else if (browserLanguage.includes('fr')) {
          return 'fr';
        } else {
          return 'en';
        }
      }

      const locale = getLocale();

      const redirectUrl = `/${locale}`;

      window.location.replace(redirectUrl);
    </script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a href="/en">Click here if you are not redirected</a>
  </body>
</html>
```

