Hello,
I am also getting the same error with "app.use" all over my tests now after migrating to the new composition API of vue-i18n.

Your solution, @th1nkgr33n, helped me for the moment – thanks ❤️. My tests are running again, i18n usage in my components is migrated, but I am getting these annoying warnings:
`[Vue warn]: Directive "t" has already been registered in target app. `


I want to use real translations for my tests (or have a config for i18n that is close to the real world), so I need the following config – ideally I want the same config as my real world app is using:
```Javascript
const i18n = createI18n({
	legacy: false,
	globalInjection: true,
	locale: "en",
	messages: {
		en: {
			...english,
		},
		de: {},
	},
});
config.global.plugins.push(i18n);
```

---

> vue-i18n made the use of the useI18n composable much stricter, not to use it outside of a
> For other purposes you need to use useNuxtApp().$i18n

Can you explain this statement in more detail?

@FruityLeo... The MarkdownEditor removed some stuff. 
What I experienced was that, the usage of the usei18n() composable inside composables is not the ideal way. This really should only be used in SFC. For other purposes you should use the useNuxtApp().$i18n

We are in on-going work to remove that warning and if we found a solution for our project, I could post that here.

For anyone wishing to mock i18n instead of using real translations, it seems the following solution could do the trick. It lets you mock the translations functions in templates and in scripts of components, and so be able to have a custom implementation for tests needing it.

```
import { beforeEach, vi } from "vitest";
import { config } from "@vue/test-utils";
import { createI18n } from "vue-i18n";

const mockTranslate = vi.fn().mockImplementation(/* Your implementation */);
const mockTranslateMultiple =   vi.fn().mockImplementation((/* Your implementation */);

beforeEach(() => {
  // Optional: restore your mock implementation if some tests change it.
});

function registerI18nPlugin() {
  // No need to pass parameters to createI18n, it seems
  const i18n = createI18n({});
  i18n.global.t = mockTranslate;
  // Add this if you use tm from i18n
  i18n.global.tm = mockTranslateMultiple;
  config.global.plugins.push(i18n);

  // Mock all i18n functions equivalent that you defined in i18n.global
  config.global.mocks = {
    $t: mockTranslate,
    $tm: mockTranslateMultiple,
  };

  // Optional: add this if you use this utils (or anyone of its friends)
  config.global.stubs = {
    "i18n-t": { template: "<div></div>" },
  };
}

registerI18nPlugin();

```

As stated @ezhyrlitsyna about warnings on "XXX has already been registered in target app", use mocks won't remove them. It seems this is due to the usage of `mountSuspended`. I haven't found any workaround about this.

To resolve this you need to set the properties using getters intead of directly passing the result of the translation function, so in the case of the reproduction project that would look like so:

```ts
useSeoMeta({
  title: () => t('homePageTitle'),
  ogTitle: () => t('homePageTitle'),
  description: () => t('aboutPageDescription'),
  ogDescription: () => t('aboutPageDescription'),
});
```

This is because during the page's setup function the locale has not yet changed to the pending locale, and the values are simply set to the resulting translations rather than a reactive translation (getter/computed) ref. 

I suppose the documentation needs to be updated to communicate that this is necessary especially when using `skipSettingLocaleOnNavigate`.

@tristan342 
Your issue sounds different from the one described here and I suggest opening a new issue with a minimal reproduction project.

