I think that's caused by the implementation in vue-leaflet.
It internally uses (LMap.vue)
```js
if (props.useGlobalLeaflet) {
      WINDOW_OR_GLOBAL.L = WINDOW_OR_GLOBAL.L || (await import("leaflet"));
}
const { map, CRS, Icon, latLngBounds, latLng, stamp }: typeof L =
      props.useGlobalLeaflet
        ? WINDOW_OR_GLOBAL.L
        : await import("leaflet/dist/leaflet-src.esm");
```
which means, that import("leaflet") loads _leaflet-src.js_, and import("leaflet/dist/leaflet-src.esm") loads _leaflet/dist/leaflet-src.esm.js_. Therefore vue-leaflet needs both versions to work correctly.

