Hi, I created a minimal reproduction:

https://github.com/naka87003/nuxt-storybook-nuxt45-repro

It reproduces the blank preview with Nuxt 4.5.2, Storybook 10.6.1, and this PR build.

I looked into this further, and this appears to be an initialization-order issue.

The reproduction uses a standard Nuxt custom `$fetch` plugin:

```ts
export default defineNuxtPlugin(() => {
  const api = $fetch.create({
    baseURL: 'https://api.example.com',
  });

  return {
    provide: {
      api,
    },
  };
});
```

When this plugin is loaded, Nuxt evaluates its generated `$fetch` module. That module creates the `$fetch` instance at module evaluation time and calls `baseURL()`.

`baseURL()` then reads `useRuntimeConfig().app`. In the Storybook preview, it appears this happens before `window.__NUXT__` has been initialized, so `useRuntimeConfig()` is undefined and `getAppConfig()` throws.

This suggests the issue is in the preview initialization performed by `@storybook-vue/nuxt`, rather than in the custom Nuxt plugin itself.

It looks like `#build/plugins` is imported statically by the preview entry. Since static ESM imports are evaluated before the entry module body runs, could the Nuxt app configuration be initialized too late for plugins that use `$fetch`?

Would delaying the `#build/plugins` import until after the preview has initialized `window.__NUXT__` be a possible fix?

