```


However, this may not work under certain conditions.

So I've been looking to solve similar problems in [Nuxt Content Assets](https://github.com/davestewart/nuxt-content-assets), and it turns out there is a way you can do this.

Nuxt Image [makes any layer's public folder accessible](https://github.com/nuxt/image/blob/main/src/ipx.ts#L31-L37) via the `_ipx` endpoint, so a hacky solution is to declare your `assets` folder as a layer, and point its public folder to itself:

```ts
// nuxt.config.ts
export default defineNuxtConfig({
  extends: [
    'assets'
  ]
})
```
```ts
// assets/nuxt.config.ts
export default defineNuxtConfig({
  dir: {
    public: __dirname
  }
})
```

I would prefer that Nuxt Image would allow an array for `dir` but this works in the meantime.

For me the solution was to put the dir-config under image.ipx.fs.dir .

```diff
 export default defineNuxtConfig({
     ...
     image: {
-      dir: process.env.NUX_IMAGES_ROOT,
+      provider: "ipx",
+      ipx: {
+        fs: { dir: process.env.NUXT_IMAGES_ROOT },
+      },
     },
     ...
   });
```

