I ran into this issue as well. As the last person to work on the AWS Amplify provider I looked into it, and it seems that Amplify's image provider will only serve a set of different sizes that were previously supplied. This can be seen [here](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amplify/latest/userguide/ssr-deployment-specification.html#deployment-manifest-imageSettings) in the docs.

With the current code, if the image size you provide is 400px, and the next largest size is 640px, the image returned will be 640px. A warning should be logged notifying you of this issue as well for any such image. 

Additionally height and width only support numbers as seen [here](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amplify/latest/userguide/integrate-image-optimization-framework.html).

Ultimately this is a limitation with AWS Amplify, and I don't know if much can be done to mitigate this.

