By default, maxAge is ignored — it takes the value from the external domain, as you can see in [this MR](https://github.com/unjs/ipx/commit/8953943942edf318afb286c60cc0a88e2a82c1b8#diff-797b7a363e29bb9ccc4d2cd6972bf144cf3b18a3bbe9a3e38b5bb5ae13f98978R59).
Luckily, [this follow-up MR](https://github.com/unjs/ipx/commit/96a8489e29103bab26665c5628b342ffdb34c009#diff-797b7a363e29bb9ccc4d2cd6972bf144cf3b18a3bbe9a3e38b5bb5ae13f98978R64) gives us a way to control that behaviour.

To make your custom maxAge actually work, you’ll need to set `ignoreCacheControl: false`:

```nuxt.config.ts
image: {
  ipx: {
    http: {
      maxAge: 60 * 60 * 24 * 365,
      ignoreCacheControl: false // <--- this one matters!
    }
  }
}
```

Unfortunately, @nuxt/image still overrides `runtimeConfig`, so you can’t set these values via env vars 😅
But static config in nuxt.config.ts works just fine.

This behaviour is still under-documented, and it would be great to have it clarified in the official documentation.

