```

comments.body:
This is technically expected behavior, the `nuxt-module-build prepare` command needs to run the module `setup` in order to generate module types.

In my experience it's best to skip throwing errors when `nuxt.options._prepare === true`, that way the module setup can still register its plugins/components/etc resulting in accurate type generation regardless of dev/prod errors.

So in the case of the repro:
```ts
// allow during type generation (nuxt prepare)
if (!discoverMePath && !_nuxt.options._prepare) {
  throw new Error('Required file discover-me.txt not found in any layer directories.')
}
```

