### Describe the feature

The assert version of [isDefined](https://vueuse.org/shared/isDefined/#isdefined).
Often when creating a page and fetching data (f.e. using `useFetch`) it is needed to show error page when there is no data or the error happened on the server. Currently we have to do something like this to assert data in the runtime and TS:
```ts
const { data, error } = await useFetch('/api/...')
if (!isDefined(data)) throw createError(error.value!)
// data value is not null here, and in the template 
// for both runtime and TS
```
As you can see we should use nullish assertion for either `data` or `error`:
I suggest to add another `assertData` util which can be used like this:
```ts
const { data, error } = await useFetch('/api/...')
assertDefined(data, error)
// data value is not null here, and in the template 
// for both runtime and TS
```
Under the hood, simplified version (for refs only):
```ts
function assertDefined<T>(data: Ref<T>, error): asserts data is Ref<Exclude<T, null | undefined>> {
  const _error = toValue(error)
  if (!toValue(data) && _error) throw createError(_error)
}
```
while I doubt whether it will somehow improve DX 🤔

Also it would be great to add an option to make `fatal = true` by default for createError. 

