### Problem

Nuxt 3.15 out of the box can transform `<NuxtLink>` and inline urls starting with `/` into absolute urls that include app's `baseURL`.

```
// In SFC Template
<img src="/images/foo.png" />

// In dev and production when baseURL = '/subfolder/'
<img src="/subfolder/images/foo.png />
```

The automatic transformation is not applied when using variables in template.

```
const imgSrc = '/images/foo.png';

// In SFC Template
<img :src="imgSrc" />

// In dev and production when baseURL = '/subfolder/'
<img src="/images/foo.png />
// No transformation applied!
``` 

### Workaround

One way to handle it is to manually retrieve `baseURL` from runtime config and add it to url:

```
const runtimeConfig = useRuntimeConfig();
const imgSrc = runtimeConfig.app.baseURL + 'images/foo.png';

<img :src="imgSrc" />
```

### Solution

To improve DX I think Nuxt should provide a composable `useMaybeAbsolutePath`, which returns a function that automatically adds `baseURL` to all paths that start with `/` and does not touch any other paths:

```ts
export default useMaybeAbsolutePath()
{
    const runtimeConfig = useRuntimeConfig();
    return (path: string) => {
        if (path.startsWith('/')) return runtimeConfig.app.baseURL + path.substring(1);
        else return path; // Do not edit relative paths and external links
    }
}
```

Usage:

```vue
<script lang="ts" setup>
const maybeAbsolutePath = useMaybeAbsolutePath();
const imgSrc = '/images/foo.png';
</script>

<template>
    <img :src="maybeAbsolutePath(imgSrc)" />
</template>
```

