This is a known trade-off that applies to all components using the `soft` and `subtle` variants (Badge, Button, Alert, Kbd, etc.), not just Badge.

We use shade `500` in light mode and `400` in dark mode for the text color of themed components (`text-{color}`). Since the `subtle` variant uses `bg-{color}/10 text-{color}`, both the text and background reference the same color, making it hard to improve contrast without decoupling them.

To meet WCAG AA (4.5:1), you'd need something like shade `700`/`200` for text only, which you can do per component through [theme overrides](https://ui.nuxt.com/docs/getting-started/theme#components):

```ts
export default defineAppConfig({
  ui: {
