**Update / Workaround**

I found a workaround by slightly bypassing the default layout structure and customizing the slot behavior.

Here's how I managed to make it work:

```vue
<UDashboardGroup unit="rem" class="bg-muted">
  <div class="flex flex-1 flex-col overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Discount Banner -->
    <AppBanner />

    <div class="relative flex h-full min-h-0 min-w-0 flex-1">
      <!-- Chats Sidebar -->
      <ChatLayoutSidebar />

      <!-- Main Content -->
      <slot />
    </div>
  </div>
</UDashboardGroup>
```

And in `app.config.ts`, I had to override some internal slot styles to adjust the layout. In particular, I had to **remove the `min-h-svh` classes** that are applied by default to the sidebar and panel, as they were preventing the layout from adapting to the height of the banner:

```ts
export default defineAppConfig({
  uiPro: {
    // Dashboard Sidebar (https://ui.nuxt.com/components/dashboard-sidebar#theme)
    dashboardSidebar: {
      slots: {
        root: 'min-h-0 shrink-0 h-full', // Removed `min-h-svh`
      }
    },
    // Dashboard Panel (https://ui.nuxt.com/components/dashboard-panel#theme)
    dashboardPanel: {
      slots: {
        root: 'relative flex flex-col min-w-0 min-h-0 shrink-0 flex-1 h-full', // Removed `min-h-svh`
      }
    }
  }
})
```

This setup allows `<AppBanner />` (or any custom banner) to appear above the dashboard and properly push the rest of the layout down without overlapping.

---

That said, it would be **really nice if the layout natively supported banners or custom top content**, without needing this kind of structural override. Maybe a dedicated slot or prop in `<UDashboardGroup />` to inject content above the dashboard layout?

This library is **absolutely fantastic** — honestly one of the best UI kits I’ve used in the Frontend ecosystem. The only real limitation I’ve hit is the **current layout rigidity**, but given the overall quality, I’m confident this will improve in future releases.

Thanks again for all your amazing work and thoughtful design! 🙏

