I did some digging using some other custom components and google AI, here is what we need to add (very simple) : 

## 1. The Props Definition (FormFieldProps)
Fix: Add them to your interface:
```typescript
export interface FormFieldProps {
  // ... existing props
  color?: FormField['variants']['color']
  variant?: FormField['variants']['variant']
}
```
## 2. The tv Function Call
Fix: Pass new props into the tailwind variant function:
```typescript
const ui = computed(() => tv({ extend: tv(theme), ...(appConfig.ui?.formField || {}) })({
  size: props.size,
  required: props.required,
  orientation: props.orientation,
  color: props.color,     // Added
  variant: props.variant  // Added
}))
```
## 3. The provide (Context Injection)
Fix: Update the injection object:
```typescript
provide(formFieldInjectionKey, computed(() => ({
  // ... existing
  size: props.size,
  color: props.color,    // Added
  variant: props.variant // Added
  // ...
}) as FormFieldInjectedOptions<FormFieldProps>))
```
## 4. Check the theme File
Ensure that #build/ui/form-field actually contains color and variant definitions in its variants object. If the base Nuxt UI theme for FormField doesn't have them, the tv function will ignore those keys even if you pass them.
in src/theme/form-field.ts
```typescript
// theme file
export default {
  // ... slots
  variants: {
    // ... size, required, orientation
    color: {
      //color examples
      primary: { label: 'text-primary-500', error: 'text-primary-400' },
      error: { label: 'text-red-500' }
    },
    variant: {
      //variant examples
      outline: { root: 'border border-gray-200 p-4 rounded-lg' },
      ghost: { root: 'bg-transparent' }
    }
  }
}
```

