The behavior you're describing is a known limitation. The documentation confirms that you can use the `expanded` prop with `v-model` to control the expandable state, but UTable doesn't currently expose a `row-key` or `getRowId` prop for stable row identification.

By default, TanStack Table (which UTable is built on) uses row indices for tracking expansion state. When rows are removed, the expansion state becomes misaligned because it still references the old index positions.

The Accordion component has a `value-key` prop for matching items, but this isn't available on UTable for row expansion. This appears to be a feature gap - the underlying TanStack Table supports `getRowId` for stable row identification, but it's not exposed through UTable's props.

As a workaround, you could manually manage the expanded state by tracking expanded item IDs:

```js
const expandedIds = ref(new Set())

// Ensure each item has a unique id
const getData = ref([
  { id: '1', title: 'one' },
  { id: '2', title: 'two' }
])

// Toggle based on id instead of using row.toggleExpanded()
function toggleExpanded(row) {
  const id = row.original.id
  if (expandedIds.value.has(id)) {
    expandedIds.value.delete(id)
  } else {
    expandedIds.value.add(id)
  }
}
```

This would require syncing the internal state with what gets displayed, but it's fragile without native row-key support.

# Main points

> There are probably still some unhandled edge cases. I'd appreciate any help finding them.

Add the following packages to `shared`:

- `reka-ui` to fix `UModal`
- `@vueuse/core` and `@vueuse/shared` to fix `useColorMode` and other stateful composables
- `@nuxt/ui/composables` to fix `useToast` state and other composables

```ts
// vite.config.ts
shared: {
  vue: {
    singleton: true,
    strictVersion: true,
  },
  'reka-ui': {
    singleton: true,
    strictVersion: true,
  },
  '@vueuse/core': {
    singleton: true,
    strictVersion: true,
  },
  '@vueuse/shared': {
    singleton: true,
    strictVersion: true,
  },
  '@nuxt/ui/composables': {
    singleton: true,
    strictVersion: true,
  },
}
```

Add a custom plugin to remove `@nuxt/ui/composables` from `optimizeDeps.include` to fix virtual imports (`#imports`) in development mode. It is added there by `@module-federation/vite`'s shared dependency mechanism.

```ts
// vite.config.ts
plugins: [
  ...(command === 'serve' ? [{
    name: 'fix-nuxt-ui-optimize-deps',
    enforce: 'post' as const,
    configResolved(config: ResolvedConfig) {
      const inc = config.optimizeDeps?.include
      if (inc) {
        const filtered = inc.filter((id) => !id.startsWith('@nuxt/ui'))
        inc.length = 0
        inc.push(...filtered)
      }
    },
  }] : []),

  ...
]
```

